@startuml
title ArcKit × Hermes Agent — MCP Interaction Sequence\n<<A non-technical user on a Mac asks her local Hermes agent to call the ArcKit MCP server\nrunning on a Linux server; Hermes guides them through framework selection, command\nidentification, and the intake questions that make those commands runnable.>>

actor "User\n(non-technical,\nMac)" as user
participant "Hermes Agent\n(local, Mac)" as hermes
participant "MCP Client\n(tool-call layer)" as mcpcl
box "Linux server" #F0FFF4
  participant "ArcKit MCP Server\n(plugin: arckit)" as mcp
  participant "architecture-workflow\nskill" as skill
  participant "Artifact Commands\n/intake engine" as cmd
end box
participant "MCP Servers\n(AWS · Azure · GCP ·\nDataCommons · govrepos · tenders)" as clouds

' ---------- 1. Kickoff ----------
user -> hermes : "I have an IT architecture project\nbut I don't know where to start —\ncan you call ArcKit?"
activate hermes
hermes -> mcpcl : request tool call:\nlist_arckit_tools()
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: tools/list
activate mcp
mcp --> mcpcl : tool catalogue\n(workflow, commands, evidence)
mcpcl --> hermes : tool catalogue
deactivate mcpcl

' ---------- 2. Framework selection ----------
hermes -> mcpcl : request tool call:\narckit.workflow.get_plan(\n  context = "new IT architecture project")
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: workflow.get_plan
mcp -> skill : activate onboarding skill
activate skill
skill -> mcp : project state?\ndeep question needed?
mcp --> skill : no projects/ dir → fresh start,\ncomplexity flag on
skill --> mcp : plan request acknowledged
deactivate skill
mcp --> mcpcl : tailored command plan\n(phase, depth, framework fit)
mcpcl --> hermes : tailored command plan
deactivate mcpcl

hermes -> user : "Based on your context the UK Gov\nframework fits best. Here is the\nrecommended command order:"
user --> hermes : "OK, sounds right"

' ---------- 3. Identify the right commands ----------
hermes -> mcpcl : request tool call:\narckit.workflow.next_step(plan)
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: workflow.next_step
activate mcp
mcp -> mcp : check artifact prerequisites\n(templates, doc control)
mcp --> mcpcl : next commands: /arckit:requirements\n→ /arckit:framework → /arckit:quality
mcpcl --> hermes : ordered command list
deactivate mcpcl

hermes -> user : "These are the commands you will run:\n1) requirements  2) framework  3) quality"
user --> hermes : "Good, let's start with requirements"

' ---------- 4. Intake questions ----------
hermes -> mcpcl : request tool call:\narckit.intake.questions(\n  command = "requirements")
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: intake.questions
activate mcp
mcp -> cmd : load requirements template\n+ intake questions
activate cmd
cmd --> mcp : question set (one at a time)
mcp --> mcpcl : question 1: "What is the\nprimary business goal?"
mcpcl --> hermes : question prompt
deactivate mcpcl

hermes -> user : "Question 1: What is the primary\nbusiness goal of this system?"
user --> hermes : "Give citizens a single portal to\napply for permits"

hermes -> mcpcl : forward answer
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: intake.answer(q1, "citizen portal")
activate mcp
mcp -> cmd : record answer, derive next question
activate cmd
cmd --> mcp : question 2: "Which stakeholders\nare involved?"
mcp --> mcpcl : question 2
mcpcl --> hermes : question prompt
deactivate mcpcl

hermes -> user : "Question 2: Which stakeholders are\ninvolved?"
user --> hermes : "Citizens, planning officers, and\nthe licensing regulator"

hermes -> mcpcl : forward answer
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: intake.answer(q2, "3 stakeholder groups")
activate mcp
mcp -> cmd : record answer; intake complete?
activate cmd
cmd --> mcp : yes — ready to render
deactivate cmd
mcp --> mcpcl : render request + answer payload
mcpcl --> hermes : render request
deactivate mcpcl

' ---------- 5. Execute command ----------
hermes -> mcpcl : request tool call:\narckit.run_command("requirements",\n  answers = {...})
activate mcpcl
mcpcl -> mcp : MCP call: commands.run
activate mcp
mcp -> cmd : invoke /arckit:requirements\nwith answers
activate cmd
cmd -> clouds : optional evidence queries\n(cloud MCP servers)
activate clouds
clouds --> cmd : evidence (e.g. AWS service fit)
deactivate clouds
cmd -> cmd : render from template →\nARC-001-REQ-v1.0.md
cmd --> mcp : artifact + summary
deactivate cmd
mcp --> mcpcl : summary + artifact path
mcpcl --> hermes : summary
deactivate mcpcl

hermes -> user : "Done — your Requirements artifact\nis saved at projects/001/ARC-001-REQ-v1.0.md.\nNext up: /arckit:framework. Continue?"
user --> hermes : "Yes"
note right of hermes
  **Pattern repeats**
  next_step → intake.questions →
  answers → run_command → artifact
end note

legend right
  | Participant | Where it runs | Role |
  |---|---|---|
  | User | Mac (browser/CLI) | Non-technical owner |
  | Hermes Agent | Mac (local) | Conversational layer; translates intent → tool calls |
  | MCP Client | Mac (local) | Serialises tool calls to MCP protocol |
  | ArcKit MCP Server | Linux server | Exposes workflow / intake / commands as MCP tools |
  | architecture-workflow | Linux server (inside ArcKit) | Onboarding triage & plan |
  | Artifact Commands | Linux server (inside ArcKit) | /arckit:* commands + intake engine |
  | Cloud MCP servers | AWS / MS / Google / … | Evidence queries during command runs |
end legend

@enduml
